          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em weak gravity conjecture
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjecture
            (
            %a{:href => "#ArkaniHamedMotlNicolisVafa06"}> Arkani-Hamed, Motl, Nicolis, Vafa 06
            ) often summarized as saying that for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            to be consistent, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/force"} force
            of the field of gravity must be weaker than that of any of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            forces, in suitable units.
          %h2#loose_statement Loose statement
          %p
            More precisely, what is argued in (
            %a{:href => "#ArkaniHamedMotlNicolisVafa06"}> AH-M-N-V 06, section 2
            ) is that there alwayst must be “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+particles"}> elementary particles
            ” for which the ratio
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m/{\vert q\vert}
            of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            over their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+charge"} electric charge
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+charge"} magnetic charge
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m/{\vert q\vert} \lt 1
            (in natural
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/units"} units
          %p
            The argument for this in (
            %a{:href => "#ArkaniHamedMotlNicolisVafa06"}> AH-M-N-V 06, section 2.2
            ) is the following. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+black+hole"} extremal
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"}> BPS state
            ) bound for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charged+black+holes"} charged black holes
            is that their mass
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %em exceeds or equals
            their charge
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert Q\vert}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M/{\vert Q\vert} \geq 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole+radiation"} black hole radiation
            any black hole is supposed to eventually decay by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radiation"} radiating
            away elementary particle quanta. If there were no elementary particle with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m/{\vert q\vert} \leq 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m/{\vert q\vert} \gt 1
            the black hole would eventually lose all its mass, while still having some non-vanishing charge left. But such “black hole remnants” have been argued to lead to inconsistency (
            %a{:href => "#Susskind96"}> Susskind 96
            ).
          %h2#in_string_theory In string theory
          %p
            The weak gravity conjecture was originally motivated from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#ArkaniHamedMotlNicolisVafa06"}> AH-M-N-V 06, section 4
            ) it is argued that the closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            excitation states in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactified
            on to 4d satisfy the condition
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m/{\vert q\vert} \lt 1
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/WeakGravityConjectureHetStates.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %h2#relation_to_cosmic_censorship Relation to cosmic censorship
          %p
            In 2015
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
            has argued that the weak gravity conjecture implies the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+censorship+hypothesis"} cosmic censorship hypothesis
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "CrisfordSantos17"} Crisford-Santos 17
          %blockquote
            %p
              Subsequent calculations by Santos and Crisford supported Vafa’s hunch; the simulations they’re running now could verify that naked singularities become cloaked in black holes right at the point where gravity becomes the weakest force. (
              %a{:href => "https://www.quantamagazine.org/where-gravity-is-weak-and-naked-singularities-are-verboten-20170620/"}> Wolchover, June 20 2017
              )
          %p
            For more on this see
            %a{:href => "#HorowitzSantos19"} Horowitz-Santos 19
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+censorship+hypothesis"} cosmic censorship hypothesis
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"} landscape of string theory vacua
          %h2#references References
          %p The statement is due to
          %ul
            %li#ArkaniHamedMotlNicolisVafa06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Arkani-Hamed"}> Nima Arkani-Hamed
              , Lubos Motl, Alberto Nicolis,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
              = succeed "," do
                %em The String Landscape, Black Holes and Gravity as the Weakest Force
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0601001"} arXiv:hep-th/0601001
          %p with reference to arguments in
          %ul
            %li#Susskind96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"}> Leonard Susskind
              ,
              %em Trouble For Remnants
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9501106"}> arXiv:hep-th/9501106
              )
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eran+Palti"}> Eran Palti
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Swampland: Introduction and Review
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06239"} arXiv:1903.06239
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Rudelius"}> Tom Rudelius
                \:
                %em An Introduction to the Weak Gravity Conjecture
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.02161"}> arXiv:2409.02161
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p#FurtherDiscussion Further discussion includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Cheung"}> Clifford Cheung
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grant+N.+Remmen"} Grant N. Remmen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Naturalness and the Weak Gravity Conjecture
                %strong 113
                051601 (2014) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1402.2287"}> arXiv:1402.2287
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.113.051601"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.113.051601
            %li
              %p
                Yu Nakayama, Yasunori Nomura,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Weak Gravity Conjecture in AdS/CFT
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.01647"} arXiv:1509.01647
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ben+Heidenreich"}> Ben Heidenreich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Reece"} Matthew Reece
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Rudelius"} Tom Rudelius
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sharpening the Weak Gravity Conjecture with Dimensional Reduction
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.06374"} arXiv:1509.06374
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Cheung"}> Clifford Cheung
                , Junyu Liu,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grant+N.+Remmen"} Grant N. Remmen
                %em Proof of the Weak Gravity Conjecture from Black Hole Entropy
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.08546"}> arXiv:1801.08546
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP10(2018)004"} doi:10.1007/JHEP10(2018)004
            %li
              %p
                Miguel Montero,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Holographic Derivation of the Weak Gravity Conjecture
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.03978"} arXiv:1812.03978
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ben+Heidenreich"}> Ben Heidenreich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Reece"} Matthew Reece
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Rudelius"} Tom Rudelius
                %em Repulsive Forces and the Weak Gravity Conjecture
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.02206"}> arXiv:1906.02206
                )
          %p
            Relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+censorship+hypothesis"} cosmic censorship hypothesis
          %ul
            %li#CrisfordSantos17
              %p
                Toby Crisford,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Santos"} Jorge Santos
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Violating weak cosmic censorship in AdS
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo
                            %mn 4
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} _4
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.05490"} arXiv:1702.05490
            %li#HorowitzSantos19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Horowitz"}> Gary Horowitz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Santos"} Jorge Santos
                %em Further evidence for the weak gravity - cosmic censorship connection
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11096"}> arXiv:1901.11096
                )
          %p
            Relation, via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+bootstrap"} conformal bootstrap
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+packing+problem"} sphere packing problem
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensions"} dimensions
            8 and 24:
          %ul
            %li#HMR19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Hartman"}> Thomas Hartman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dalimil+Maz%C3%A1%C4%8D"} Dalimil Mazáč
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Rastelli"} Leonardo Rastelli
              %em Sphere Packing and Quantum Gravity
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.01319"}> arXiv:1905.01319
              )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Lars Aalsma,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Cole"} Alex Cole
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Shiu"} Gary Shiu
              %em A New Spin on the Weak Gravity Conjecture
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.05337"}> arXiv:2011.05337
              )
          %p
            Proof of the weak gravity conjecture in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string+theory"} bosonic string theory
            is claimed in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ben+Heidenreich"}> Ben Heidenreich
              , Matteo Lotito,
              %em Proving the Weak Gravity Conjecture in Perturbative String Theory, Part I: The Bosonic String
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.14449"}> arXiv:2401.14449
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Yong Xiao, Qiang Wang, Aonan Zhang:
              %em A Proof of the Weak Gravity Conjecture via Leading-Order Quantum Gravity Effects
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.08459"}> arXiv:2503.08459
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            In relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amplituhedron"} positivity
            relations among
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
          %ul
            %li
              Tran Quang Loc:
              %em Exploring amplitude criteria for weak gravity in electroweak theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.01497"}> arXiv:2505.01497
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
